{"id": "EUVD-2026-71282", "enisaUuid": "f5cccee2-e386-35be-a9d9-757fd01bac4f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: qce - fix CCM AAD buffer underallocation\n\nThe AAD buffer allocated in qce_aead_ccm_prepare_buf_assoclen()\ncan be smaller than the length later programmed into the DMA\nscatterlist.\n\nThe allocation size is currently calculated as:\n\n  ALIGN(assoclen, 16) + MAX_CCM_ADATA_HEADER_LEN\n\nwhile the DMA length is set to:\n\n  ALIGN(assoclen + adata_header_len, 16)\n\nSince ALIGN() does not distribute over addition, the allocation\ncan be smaller than the DMA length. For example, when\nassoclen = 32 and adata_header_len = 2:\n\n  allocation = ALIGN(32, 16) + 6 = 38\n  DMA length = ALIGN(32 + 2, 16) = 48\n\nAs a result, the QCE hardware can read beyond the allocated\nbuffer while computing the CBC-MAC over the associated data.\nThe extra bytes are folded into the authentication tag,\nresulting in an incorrect tag and causing CCM self-test\nfailures such as:\n\n  alg: aead: ccm-aes-qce encryption test failed (wrong result)\n  on test vector 8\n\nFix the allocation by adding the maximum possible AAD header\nlength before alignment:\n\n  ALIGN(assoclen + MAX_CCM_ADATA_HEADER_LEN, 16)\n\nThis guarantees that the allocated buffer is large enough\nfor the fully padded AAD data for all supported header sizes.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:54:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11775b35ce9f27e73d62188d7d38aa0dc0a219aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c9e0f06a023107694698a7930616aeb460d91816", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc56d2b0d77cfeea061e98114992ee687d5eb4dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/002f1f99aef7ea631cb687fc17bce64e4963f6aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f65718b9c1095eef1ae9b374aa0384b1b083f3c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46a84efe2dbaddde89073a3c00c694486937c34b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4839f4c21f9c577eedef2919ced878a3057c7fc3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f2345f47dd189625f657cd72437179ab4170ee1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80832", "GHSA-5ch2-359f-fp8j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16be505c-e72d-3be5-99ba-8f2b172028e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9363efb4181c5e0fbf86bdfa759262aa29f0eb50 <4839f4c21f9c577eedef2919ced878a3057c7fc3"}, {"id": "1ef298a9-2070-35b0-9191-4da86a85f9c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3288b710-705e-3e43-adb2-e1e6c682a34c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.108"}, {"id": "335539a4-0a3b-3829-a6da-8425d10d5d0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "473733e5-a850-3940-af32-8bd2e17f3dae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9363efb4181c5e0fbf86bdfa759262aa29f0eb50 <cc56d2b0d77cfeea061e98114992ee687d5eb4dd"}, {"id": "4fdeec24-4f96-3f56-808b-c93e41e10f77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}, {"id": "63e2eb93-222e-3b0e-8f1e-e8857fbba9ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9363efb4181c5e0fbf86bdfa759262aa29f0eb50 <11775b35ce9f27e73d62188d7d38aa0dc0a219aa"}, {"id": "69f0c57f-b707-3c91-98e9-f5d3dfd11827", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9363efb4181c5e0fbf86bdfa759262aa29f0eb50 <7f2345f47dd189625f657cd72437179ab4170ee1"}, {"id": "6b636b8e-b2f3-342e-b071-990987a46b14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9363efb4181c5e0fbf86bdfa759262aa29f0eb50 <46a84efe2dbaddde89073a3c00c694486937c34b"}, {"id": "7585b7f5-499f-3a81-8128-e7622dc7c90d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9363efb4181c5e0fbf86bdfa75